": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "type": "RSLT"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "enpe7n4le01ob04re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n4le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "100", "text": "<strong>Sarah:</strong> Hey, Jason! How's everything?</br>\n<strong>Jason:</strong> Hi, Sarah! Not bad, I guess\u2026</br>\n<strong>Sarah:</strong> Hmm\u2026 Why do you say that?</br>\n<strong>Jason:</strong> Well, I have to prepare a presentation about software programming. I found a lot of information but now I don't know how to organize it.</br>\n<strong>Sarah:</strong> Wow! That requires a lot of research, Who are you working with?</br>\n<strong>Jason:</strong> A classmate, but he is busy now. </br>\n<strong>Sarah:</strong> You're in luck!  I made a similar presentation last semester. I can help you. So, what kind of information do you need?</br>\n<strong>Jason:</strong> I need to explain the main key features of software programming in the 80's.</br>", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "40800", "text": "<strong>Sarah:</strong>  Let's start! The first key feature was the Analytical Engine.</br>\n<strong>Jason:</strong> What was the Analytical Engine for?</br>\n<strong>Sarah:</strong> It made calculations with Bernoulli numbers. And, it is often considered as the first computer program in the world. On the other hand, the Turing Machine was one of the first machines to store data.</br>\n<strong>Jason:</strong> Wow! Who did you learn with? </br>\n<strong>Sarah:</strong> I had an excellent professor, his name is Mr. Morris. Actually, I learned a lot about imperative languages too.</br>", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "73500", "text": "<strong>Jason:</strong> What is that for?</br>\n<strong>Sarah:</strong> During that time, a relative consolidation was very important, so programmers had many new ideas. In fact, they found an interesting way to give commands to computers in order to perform particular tasks. It was the imperative language, which basically consisted in describing how a program had to operate.</br>\n<strong>Jason:</strong> Hmm, I see. That's why it's called imperative language.</br>\n<strong>Sarah:</strong> Exactly! Another important key feature you need to know is about the fifth-generation programming languages, sometimes abbreviated as (5GL). Programmers built special programs that could solve problems by themselves, without the need of a programmer. That's why nowadays common users don't have to create algorithms or implement complex tasks in a computer. As you can see, 5GL was the beginning of artificial intelligence.", "image": "enpe7n4le01ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le01ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}